OL,3,GNEWSAWomen feel 'unsafe' in town
OL,4,Acentres after dark
OL,5,
OL,6,FOn one evening in Middlesbrough, the
OL,7,FBBC spoke to young women about how they
OL,8,Fstay safe after a survey by the area's
OL,9,FPolice and Crime Commissioner (PCC)
OL,10,Frevealed that most on Teesside feel
OL,11,Funsafe in public places after dark.
OL,13,FFor Zoe and her friend Beth, who are in
OL,14,Fthe town for a meal together, they have
OL,15,Fsimilar practices.
OL,17,FZoe describes using her phone or
OL,18,Ftexting a friend so that people know
OL,19,Fshe has "someone who cares" about where
OL,20,Fshe is.
